                <pb facs="pm_d10-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d10-1"/>

                <head>PM–10. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>In a series of notes from Ambassador Julian F. Harrington in Panama, to Foreign
                    Minister Moreno, on February 17, March 23, and September 22, 1959, the United
                    States Government informed the Republic of Panama of its desire to amend the
                    United States Army Mission agreement of July 7, 1942, as extended. In his reply
                    of November 6, 1959, Moreno accepted the American proposals, and the agreement
                    entered into force on November 6, 1959. For the texts of the notes exchanged,
                    see 12 UST 718. Documentation concerning the negotiation of this agreement is in
                    Department of State file 719.58.</p>
            </div>
